   "created_at": "2026-11-18T00:54:02Z",
   "updated_at": "2026-11-18T00:54:02Z",
   "body": "/claim cloud/i970-sonnet\n\nPlan:\n- Reproduce on Linux: the failing job shows every test of the run « passed after 58.5 seconds », i.e. the whole process stalled ~58 s (the same stall `dev-swift` shows); `LoopbackServer`'s `hangs` replies sleep 5 s then close, so after a stall longer than 5 s the server's close can reach the client before the idle watcher fires. I reproduce it by stopping the test process (SIGSTOP/SIGCONT) for more than 5 s, not by guessing, then in a loop under CPU load.\n- Fix the cause: a silent test server must never close first (hold the connection until the client closes it); check whether the transport also needs a mapping for a failure after the idle deadline, and whether my « stalled process » reset in the watcher (#1009) makes it worse.\n- A test pins the mapping or the server behaviour; 200 consecutive green runs under load, shown; macOS: no change to the Apple path.\n- Draft PR, Opus review, hand-off on #893.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
